D5:
Leaks: (1) A new Heartbeat connection is created on every CharacterAdded and never disconnected; after each respawn the old ones keep running on dead characters (holding references to destroyed models, so they are never GC'd), and the per-frame cost grows with every death. (2) sessions[player] is never cleared, so every player who ever joined (Player object + history) stays in memory; history is also unbounded. (3) Connections to player.CharacterAdded are fine once the Player is destroyed, but the strong table reference keeps it alive. Fixes:

local auraConns = {}
Players.PlayerAdded:Connect(function(player)
  sessions[player] = { kills = 0, history = {} }
  player.CharacterAdded:Connect(function(char)
    if auraConns[player] then auraConns[player]:Disconnect() end
    auraConns[player] = RunService.Heartbeat:Connect(function() updateAura(char) end)
    char.Destroying:Once(function() if auraConns[player] then auraConns[player]:Disconnect(); auraConns[player] = nil end end)
  end)
end)
Players.PlayerRemoving:Connect(function(player)
  if auraConns[player] then auraConns[player]:Disconnect(); auraConns[player] = nil end
  sessions[player] = nil
end)

Cap history (ring buffer / trim old entries). Better still: one global Heartbeat loop iterating active characters. Set workspace.PlayerCharacterDestroyBehavior = Enabled so old characters are destroyed.
